    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d609">

                <pb facs="0967" n="1925" xml:id="pg1925"/>

                <head>No. 47.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby
                        to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-09-21"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 21,
                        1887</date>. (Received November 11.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 458.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Adverting to my dispatch No. 453, of date
                    the 15th instant, I have now the honor to inclose copy of reply which I received
                    from the foreign office, wherein you will observe that the Chinese Government
                    find it difficult to accept the invitation of the Government of the United
                    States, for the reasons set forth therein, to cooperate with it in carrying out,
                    upon a reciprocal basis, the act of Congress approved June 19, 1886, having
                    relation to the abolition of tonnage dues and other charges on navigation.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d609-a1.xml" xpointer="d609-a1"/>
            </div>
